From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 08 Sep 2026 06:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: report the BSSID of each link in debugfs

The bssid file of a station interface reports the default link. An MLO
association keeps a BSSID per link and never uses the default link, so
the file reads as the zero address and gives no way to tell which BSSID
belongs to which link.

Add a bssid file to each link directory. The link directories already
carry the local address of the link, so this completes the pair.

Add it in ieee80211_link_debugfs_add() rather than in add_link_files().
The latter also runs for the default link with the netdev directory,
where a bssid file already exists.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/net/mac80211/debugfs_netdev.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/debugfs_netdev.c
@@ -735,6 +735,7 @@ static ssize_t ieee80211_if_parse_active
 IEEE80211_IF_FILE_RW(active_links);
 
 IEEE80211_IF_LINK_FILE(addr, conf->addr, MAC);
+IEEE80211_IF_LINK_FILE(link_bssid, u.mgd.bssid, MAC);
 
 #ifdef CPTCFG_MAC80211_MESH
 IEEE80211_IF_FILE(estab_plinks, u.mesh.estab_plinks, ATOMIC);
@@ -1060,6 +1061,11 @@ void ieee80211_link_debugfs_add(struct i
 				   link->sdata->vif.debugfs_dir);
 
 	DEBUGFS_ADD(link->debugfs_dir, addr);
+
+	if (link->sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
+		debugfs_create_file("bssid", 0400, link->debugfs_dir, link,
+				    &link_link_bssid_ops);
+
 	add_link_files(link, link->debugfs_dir);
 }
 
